{"name":"Iguana","hex":"#878757","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Iguana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Iguanidae – the iguanas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Iguana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iguana","blocks":[{"text":"Iguana is a genus of herbivorous lizards that are native to tropical areas of Mexico, Central America, South America, and the Caribbean. The genus was first described by Austrian naturalist J.N. Laurenti in 1768. Two species are placed in the genus: The green iguana, which is widespread throughout its range and a popular pet; and the Lesser Antillean iguana, which is native to the Lesser Antilles. Genetic analysis indicates that the green iguana may comprise a complex of multiple species, some of which have been recently described, but the Reptile Database considers all of these as subspecies of the green iguana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Green_Iguana_In_Florida.jpg/330px-Green_Iguana_In_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iguana","wikidata":"Q205531"},{"title":"Iguana (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Iguana is a 1988 American adventure crime film directed by Monte Hellman and starring Everett McGill in the main role. It is based on the novel by Spanish author Alberto Vázquez-Figueroa, itself based on the life of a real Irish sailor called Patrick Watkins. The film was mainly shot on location in Lanzarote. Monte Hellman won Bastone Bianco Award for this movie on the Venice Film Festival in 1988. Iguana premiered in theaters on April 1, 1988, and was released on DVD on January 30, 2001, via Anchor Bay Entertainment. The film ends with the titles \"For Warren\" as Hellman dedicated the film to his friend Warren Oates."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Iguana_dvd_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iguana_(film)","wikidata":"Q4197772"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg/500px-Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg/1280px-Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg/500px-Male_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A male green iguana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMale_Green_Iguana_Belize.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Iguana-001.jpg/500px-Iguana-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Iguana-001.jpg/1280px-Iguana-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Iguana-001.jpg/500px-Iguana-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iguana eating flower.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIguana-001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Iguana_iguana_eating_Mangifera_indica_from_Venezuela.jpg/500px-Iguana_iguana_eating_Mangifera_indica_from_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Iguana_iguana_eating_Mangifera_indica_from_Venezuela.jpg/1280px-Iguana_iguana_eating_Mangifera_indica_from_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm